  "description": "The Coast Guard located and medevaced a 48-year-old man aboard an overdue 23-foot pleasure craft on the Pungo River near Swan Quarter, N.C., Saturday, Sept. 15, 2012. The Jayhawk crew located the overdue boat aground at approximately 6 a.m., medevaced the man reportedly suffering from a laceration and a leg injury and took him to Vidant Beaufort Hospital in Washington, N.C. U.S. Coast Guard video by Coast Guard Air Station Elizabeth City",
